; Three rooms, each with one corner whose position states no accuracy or is
; otherwise not what a measurement can read.
;
; site:S-01's third corner was taken off a drawing with no accuracy stated.
; Specification section 6.5 makes that claim unrankable rather than absent: it
; cannot win resolution, and it is still the answer where nothing rankable was
; said. The room is measured from it, and its budget is unknown and names that
; corner as why. Nothing about that room is a diagnostic.
;
; site:S-11's corners were surveyed in feet, in a frame in metres. Nothing
; converts, so a measurement reading them under the imperial predicate reads
; none of them and says the unit is why — the one case in which it is. One
; reading under the metric predicate finds nothing claimed, and says that.
;
; site:S-21's third corner was taped twice, with no accuracy stated either time.
; Two unrankable claims are ambiguity rather than an unranked answer, so that
; corner is placed nowhere, and the diagnostic says so rather than blaming a
; unit.
(node
  site:S-01
  (label "Taped room")
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area)
  (frame frame:building)
  (boundary geom:L-01))
(node
